===============================================================================
WHAT THE MIT LICENCE ABOVE COVERS — AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
===============================================================================

The MIT licence above covers THIS PROJECT'S OWN WORK: the simulator's source
code, its stylesheets, its hand-drawn SVG artwork, its documentation and the
MaestroPCA Arduino library.

It cannot, and does not, grant you rights over the parts of this repository
that belong to other people. A licence can only give away what the licensor
owns. Read CREDITS.md; the short version:

  1. THE 3D GEOMETRY IS NOT MIT LICENSED.
     The MK4 astromech and the Polar Mouse (src/js/cad/payload.js,
     src/js/cad/mouse-payload.js, and any .r2m derived from them) are
     MrBaddeley's paid Patreon designs, included here WITH HIS PERMISSION.

     That permission is for this project to publish them. It does not travel
     to you. You may run and modify this simulator. You may NOT extract,
     print, repackage, redistribute or sell the geometry. If you want the
     models, buy them from him: https://www.patreon.com/mrbaddeley

     If you fork this repository and republish it, ask him yourself first.

  2. THE PADAWAN360 FIRMWARE LINEAGE IS BSD-3-CLAUSE, and stays BSD-3-Clause.
     The .ino files under tests/fixtures-sketches/ are upstream sketches kept
     verbatim, with their own copyright headers. Copyright (c) Dan Kraus and
     the padawan360 contributors. https://github.com/dankraus/padawan360

  3. THREE.JS IS MIT, copyright (c) three.js authors, vendored in
     src/vendor/three.min.js. https://threejs.org

  4. THE BOARD PHOTOGRAPHS belong to their manufacturers — Pololu, Arduino,
     Adafruit, Dimension Engineering, Flipsky, DY and others — and are
     reproduced small, for identification. They are not licensed onward. Every
     card falls back to a drawn stand-in if a photograph is removed
     (src/art/boards/README.md).

Star Wars, R2-D2 and related marks are Lucasfilm's. This is a non-commercial
fan project with no connection to, or endorsement from, Lucasfilm or The Walt
Disney Company.
